  "note": "Borough election polled Wednesday 17 May 1961 and counted on Thursday 18 May: eighteen candidates for the three aldermanships and twelve councillorships. The new council was twelve Unionists and three Independents, against thirteen and two before. Labels as printed: U Unionist, I Independent. Turnout not printed. Aldermen were elected for six years; George Hill, the former Mayor, stood as an Independent and topped the poll."
